2319|n|The act of drawing, or the state of being drawn; as, the traction of a muscle. ; Specifically, the act of drawing a body along a plane by motive power, as the drawing of a carriage by men or horses, the towing of a boat by a tug. ; Attraction; a drawing toward. ; The adhesive friction of a wheel on a rail, a rope on a pulley, or the like.	a:1b5y,31,7;1awf,18,7;1w1v,16,6~1b5y,31,7;1awf,18,7;1w1v,16,6	v:tx0,94,5;tww,87,3;twt,60,2;uov,22,4~tx0,94,5;uov,22,4;tww,87,3;twt,60,2	n:twt,60,2~twt,60,2
