23pb|n|That branch of mathematics which treats of the relations of the sides and angles of triangles, which the methods of deducing from certain given parts other required parts, and also of the general relations which exist between the trigonometrical functions of arcs or angles. ; A treatise in this science.	a:6gk,74,3~6gk,74,3
23q8|n|According to the French notation, which is used upon the Continent generally and in the United States, the number expressed by a unit with twelve ciphers annexed; a million millions; according to the English notation, the number produced by involving a million to the third power, or the number represented by a unit with eighteen ciphers annexed. See the Note under Numeration.	N:18vi,120,3~18vi,120,3
23ql|n|Dress; gear; ornaments. ; Order; disposition; condition; as, to be in good trim. ; The state of a ship or her cargo, ballast, masts, etc., by which she is well prepared for sailing. ; The lighter woodwork in the interior of a building; especially, that used around openings, generally in the form of a molded architrave, to protect the plastering at those points.	N:1km5,108,2~1km5,108,2
23ql|a|Dress; gear; ornaments. ; Order; disposition; condition; as, to be in good trim. ; The state of a ship or her cargo, ballast, masts, etc., by which she is well prepared for sailing. ; The lighter woodwork in the interior of a building; especially, that used around openings, generally in the form of a molded architrave, to protect the plastering at those points.	j:1km5,108,2~1km5,108,2
